-- title:
--   §2, p. 5 — the closed-form filter Y_t is a version of E[D | F̄^S_t]
-- statement:
--   Let $x>0$ and $y\in[0,1]$, let $S^x$ be the asset (2.1) with prior $\mathbb P(D^y=1)=y$, and let $\overline{\mathcal F}^S_t$ be the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $(S^x_s)_{s\le t}$ and the null sets. For every $t\ge0$,
--   $$Y^y_t=\frac{y\,\ell_t}{y\,\ell_t+1-y}=\mathbb E\big[D^y\,\big|\,\overline{\mathcal F}^S_t\big]\quad\mathbb P\text{-a.s.},$$
--   where $\ell_t=\exp\big(-\frac{\delta_0}{\sigma^2}\ln\frac{S^x_t}{x}+\frac{\delta_0}{2\sigma^2}(2r-\delta_0-\sigma^2)t\big)$.
--
--   The paper defines its belief process $D^y_t$ as an adapted càdlàg version of this conditional expectation (p. 5). The explicit Bayes posterior used here is adapted to the observation filtration and has continuous paths.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Path continuity implies the paper's càdlàg requirement.
-- source:
--   De Angelis, Gensbittel, Villeneuve, A Dynkin Game on Assets with Incomplete Information on the Return, arXiv:1705.07352v4, p. 5, §2 (definition of D^y_t)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DynkinIncInfo_Saddle_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace DynkinIncInfo.Saddle

/-- De Angelis, Gensbittel, Villeneuve, A Dynkin Game on Assets with Incomplete Information on the Return, arXiv:1705.07352v4, p. 5, Section 2 (filter identity): the process `D^y_t` is a version of the
martingale `E⁰_y[D | 𝓕̄^S_t]`.

For `x > 0`, `y ∈ [0, 1]` and every `t ≥ 0`, the closed-form filter
`Y_t = y ℓ_t / (y ℓ_t + 1 − y)` is almost surely equal to the conditional expectation of `D^y`
given the observation σ-algebra `𝓕̄^S_t`.

**Formalization Note.** This item ties the explicit filter `Y` used throughout the mission to the
paper's definition of `D^y_t`. `𝓕̄^S` is generated by `(S_s)_{s ≤ t}` and all `P`-null
sets, using the completeness field of `Setting`. The statement also records adaptedness
and path continuity; continuity implies the paper's càdlàg property. -/
theorem filter_condexp {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (p : Params) (st : Setting Ω)
    (x y : ℝ) (hx : 0 < x) (hy : y ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (t : ℝ≥0) :
    Y p st x y t =ᵐ[st.P] st.P[D st y | FS p st x y t] ∧
    Measurable[FS p st x y t] (Y p st x y t) ∧
    (∀ ω : Ω, Continuous (fun s : ℝ≥0 => Y p st x y s ω)) := by sorry

end DynkinIncInfo.Saddle
